cmd.resolve.pin.long:
A pin is written as pinned / confidence 100 / source review, and automatic runs never change it afterwards; with an id, capy first reads that track from the platform to make sure it exists, and adds its ISRC to
the alias set. If the id (or its ISRC) already belongs to another cid, the two are the same recording: after you confirm, they are merged per decision 21 (the lexicographically smaller cid wins and every playlist item is repointed to it);
without a TTY this needs --yes, otherwise it exits 2 and writes nothing.
